title: UGT Militia
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: reichsbanner_timer <= 0 and not ugt_militia_banned
card-image: img/es/events/asturias_1934.jpg
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; reichsbanner_timer += 6; ugt_militia_cost = 2 if ugt_militia_militancy > 0.15 else ugt_militia_cost = 1; ugt_militia_cost = 3 if ugt_militia_militancy > 0.3
max-visits: 6
subtitle: Paramilitary organizing in defense of the republic.

= UGT Militia

The <span style="color: #700000;">**UGT Militia**</span> is a mass organization for the defense of the Republic against the extremists who threaten it - most of its cadres are drawn from the <span style="color: #700000;">**UGT**</span>'s own membership, with a smaller <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> contingent. Some would call it a paramilitary, although currently it is hardly any sort of military.

[? if industrial_psoe < 46 or industrial_psoe < industrial_falange or industrial_psoe < industrial_pce : The militia is having a more difficult time recruiting, as the <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> is no longer the dominant party among the workers. Many of its members have left. ?]

- @militant: Fund more military-style training and equipment for the militia.
- @militant_2: Use our existing resources to support more training for the militia.
- @same: Keep the militia as it is.
- @cut_rb: Cut funding for the militia.
- @women_militia
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@militant
choose-if: resources >= ugt_militia_cost
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources ([+ ugt_militia_cost +] needed).
subtitle: -[+ ugt_militia_cost +] resources
on-arrival: resources -= ugt_militia_cost; ugt_militia_strength += 100; ugt_militia_militancy += 0.05; left_strength += 2; left_dissent -= 2; reformist_dissent += 5; industrial_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); ceda_relation -= 3 if strife < 5; izq_rep_relation -= 3 if strife < 5

Some in our party decry the increasing militarization of the UGT Militia. They say it risks provoking the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CEDA**</span>'s own paramilitary sympathies, or alienating our republican allies. On the other hand, more militant workers are being lured to our organization, away from the <span style="color: #333333;">**CNT**</span>.

[? if strife < 5: The <span style="color: #7B2D8E;">**Republican Left**</span> is uneasy about the militarization of the UGT Militia. ?][? if strife >= 5: Seeing the strife that has filled Spain's streets, the <span style="color: #7B2D8E;">**Republican Left**</span> and <span style="color: #E8B23A;">Radicals</span> seem convinced that it is necessary, and mute their criticisms. ?]


@militant_2
view-if: funded_reichsbanner >= 1
on-arrival: ugt_militia_militancy += 0.02; funded_reichsbanner -= 1

As we have already funded resources towards the militia, we can invest in building up their militancy.


@same

The UGT Militia is already serving the purpose it needs to serve. There is no reason to change what already works.

- @return: Continue...


@cut_rb
subtitle: +1 resources
on-arrival: resources += 1; ugt_militia_strength -= 100; ugt_militia_militancy -= 0.05; left_strength -= 2; left_dissent -= 2; industrial_pce += 2; unemployed_pce += 2

Cutting resources to the militia causes a drop in the membership, and leads some would-be members to join the <span style="color: #8a0303;">**PCE**</span> instead.


@women_militia
title: Allow women to join the UGT Militia.
subtitle: -1 resources - This might cause a backlash from existing members.
choose-if: resources > 0
view-if: womens_rights >= 4 and iron_front_formed == 1 and women_in_militia == 0
on-arrival: resources -= 1; ugt_militia_militancy *= 0.85; ugt_militia_strength += 400; women_in_militia = 1
max-visits: 1
achievement: women_reichsbanner

The suggestion to allow women into the militia is ridiculed by most, but this is an exceptional time, and we need anyone who is willing to join. We organize specialized units for women.

After allowing women to join, the number of comrades who leave is more than balanced out by the number of radicalized women and others who join. However, many of our departed members were veterans, and many of the new members have no experience with military-style training.
